      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Typing Props and Children",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Typing Props",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Type props with an ==interface== or `type` on the destructured parameter",
                "Annotate the parameter; skip `React.FC`",
                "Optional prop: `?`; default goes in the destructuring",
                "A missing required prop fails at {red:compile time}"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "tsx",
              "lines": [
                "interface CardProps { title: string; count?: number }",
                "function Card({ title, count = 0 }: CardProps) {",
                "  return <h2>{title} {count}</h2>;",
                "}",
                "// <Card />  -> error: 'title' is missing"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. children and Native Props",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Accepts"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`React.ReactNode`",
                  "string, number, element, array, null, fragment"
                ],
                [
                  "`React.ReactElement`",
                  "one JSX element only (stricter)"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Wrapper: ==ComponentPropsWithoutRef<'button'>== (or `extends` it)",
                "Forwards `onClick`, `disabled` and the rest via `...rest`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "tsx",
              "lines": [
                "type BtnProps = React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<'button'>",
                "  & { variant?: string };",
                "function Btn({ variant, ...rest }: BtnProps) {",
                "  return <button {...rest} />;",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`children: React.JSX.Element` rejects strings and `null`",
                "`any` for props turns off checking",
                "Function prop with no signature; write `onSelect: (id: string) => void`"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Typing State and Events",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Typing State and Events",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Typing useState",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`useState(0)` infers ==number== from the initial value",
                "Initial value narrower than the real type: `useState<User | null>(null)`",
                "Empty arrays need an explicit generic, else the type is ==never[]=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "tsx",
              "lines": [
                "const [n, setN] = useState(0);",
                "const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null);",
                "const [tags, setTags] = useState<string[]>([]);"
              ],
              "note": "n is number, user is User | null, tags is string[]"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Event Types",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Event",
                "Type"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Input change",
                  "`React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>`"
                ],
                [
                  "Click",
                  "`React.MouseEvent<HTMLButtonElement>`"
                ],
                [
                  "Submit",
                  "`React.FormEvent<HTMLFormElement>`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Inline** handler: event type is ==inferred== from context",
                "**Separate** handler: annotate the event yourself",
                "`React.ChangeEventHandler<HTMLInputElement>` types the whole function"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Refs and Reducers",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null)`: `.current` may be ==null==, check before use",
                "@types/react 19: `.current` is **writable**; it was read-only in 18",
                "`useReducer` takes a ==discriminated union== of actions, so each `case` narrows"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "tsx",
              "lines": [
                "type Action = { type: 'add'; id: string } | { type: 'clear' };",
                "switch (a.type) {",
                "  case 'add': return [...s, a.id]; // a.id is string",
                "  case 'clear': return [];",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Common mistake",
              "text": "`useState([])` is ==never[]==. Always write the generic: `useState<string[]>([])`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Generic Components",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Generic Components",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Declaring and Constraining T",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Declare a ==type parameter== on the function: `function List<T>(...)`",
                "`T` is **inferred** from the `items` you pass in",
                "`render` receives the same `T`, so `item` is fully typed"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "tsx",
              "lines": [
                "function List<T>({ items, render }: {",
                " items: T[];",
                " render: (item: T) => React.ReactNode;",
                "}) {",
                " return <ul>{items.map((x, i) => <li key={i}>{render(x)}</li>)}</ul>;",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "T inferred from items"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Add `extends` so the body can rely on fields",
                "`<T extends { id: string }>` lets you use ==item.id== as the `key`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Generic Hooks",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Generic hooks ==pass the type through==",
                "`function useFetch<T>(url: string)` returns `{ data: T | null }`",
                "Caller sets it: `useFetch<User[]>('/api/users')`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Gotchas in .tsx",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Problem",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Bare arrow `<T>` parses as {red:JSX}",
                  "`<T,>` or `<T extends unknown>`"
                ],
                [
                  "Or avoid it entirely",
                  "Use a {green:function declaration}"
                ],
                [
                  "`React.memo` / `forwardRef` ==erase== generics",
                  "Cast the result, or wrap in a function declaration to keep `T`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "In .tsx, write ==<T,>== for arrow generics. Wrapping with memo or forwardRef **loses T** unless you cast."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
