    {
      "title": "React TypeScript Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "React TypeScript Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Props, State, Refs",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "tsx",
              "lines": [
                "interface Props {",
                "  title: string;",
                "  children?: React.ReactNode;",
                "  onSelect: (id: string) => void;",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "Annotate the parameter, not React.FC"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "Write"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Nullable state",
                  "`useState<User | null>(null)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Array state",
                  "`useState<string[]>([])` (else `never[]`)"
                ],
                [
                  "DOM ref",
                  "`useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null)`, `.current` may be {red:null}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Events and Generics",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Element",
                "Event type"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Input",
                  "`React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>`"
                ],
                [
                  "Button click",
                  "`React.MouseEvent<HTMLButtonElement>`"
                ],
                [
                  "Form submit",
                  "`React.FormEvent<HTMLFormElement>`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Inline handlers ==infer== the event; separate ones need the type",
                "Constraint: `<T extends { id: string }>` lets you use `item.id`",
                "In .tsx a bare `<T>` parses as JSX: write ==`<T,>`==",
                "`React.memo` and `forwardRef` erase generics"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Vite and Tooling",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "npm create vite@latest app -- --template react-ts",
                "npx tsc -b --noEmit"
              ],
              "note": "Vite only strips types; tsc does the type-check"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Env vars need the ==VITE_== prefix: `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL`",
                "Lint: ==rules-of-hooks== (error) + ==exhaustive-deps== (warn)",
                "Profiler: enable **Record why each component rendered**"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "text": "Why `children: React.ReactNode`, not `JSX.Element`? Node accepts strings and null. Why does Vite miss type errors? It never checks types."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
